Root cause: freshCacheModuleId resolved null (ModuleCacheIdentityHelper.resolveCachedModuleRaw
returned no cached pref -- this session never wrote one, matching the AC's own premise "the
cached identity-scoped module pref [is] also null"). _clearCartOnline has NO fallback tier for
this state (unlike _removeCartItemOnline's fallbackModuleId, sourced from the removed item's own
module_id) -- the module header is correctly omitted per NEARS-2556 but the backend
(Admin/app/Http/Controllers/Api/V1/CartController.php:319-324, remove_cart) fails CLOSED on a
missing header by design (NEARS-771): `$moduleId === null` -> 400 `messages.module_id_required`
= "Module id required".

Consequences (all three verified live):
1. AC2 FAILS: DELETE /api/v1/customer/cart/remove returned 400, not 200.
2. AC1 FAILS: cart is NOT emptied server-side. DB cross-check (multi_food_db.carts, guest
   user_id=1332) after the whole flow completed and the module switch to Food & Restaurant (2)
   had already gone through:
     id=681 item_id=59 module_id=1 user_id=1332 is_guest=1 quantity=1 updated_at=2026-09-02 05:38:40
   (updated_at == the original add-to-cart time; never touched by a delete.)
3. NEW finding beyond the AC's literal text: the UI's Basket tab shows "Your cart is empty"
   (screenshot: bug-clearcart-null-module-400-false-empty.png) -- a FALSE-empty state, not an
   honest error. The subsequent /customer/cart/list GET rides the NEW module (2) header (module
   switch already happened per the guard's load-bearing ordering), so the orphaned module-1 row
   is silently excluded from the response and never surfaces to the user -- worse than a visible
   error: a stuck, invisible, still-billable cart row survives the "Clear Cart" action.
4. AC3 FAILS: _clearCartOnline's apiClient.deleteData call does not pass handleError:false, so
   ApiChecker.checkApi (lib/api/api_checker.dart) runs its default non-2xx path:
   `showCustomSnackBar(response.statusText, ...)`, where response.statusText carries the
   backend's raw errors[0].message body verbatim (per api_client.dart's own NEARS-482/handleResponse
   comment) -- i.e. the literal backend string "Module id required" is shown to the user via
   snackbar. (Snackbar not independently screenshot-captured this run -- GetX/Flutter snackbars
   paint outside the a11y tree per the documented gotcha, NEARS-1099 -- but the code path is
   unambiguous and unconditional for this exact response shape: no branch suppresses statusText
   for a 400 here.)

AC4 (regression, normal already-has-module Clear Cart) not exercised live this run because
reaching the null-module repro state consumed the session's only "never entered a module" window;
the automated backstop (cart_repository_clear_cart_module_identity_test.dart, "AC4 regression"
case) already pins this branch and is not implicated by the finding above (different code branch:
`ModuleHelper.getModule()?.id == null` is false in the normal-module case, so `_clearCartOnline`
never enters the null-fallback branch discussed here).

